      "content": "Focusing on pathways to citizenship and humanitarian processing is generally considered more likely to provide a long-term, stable solution. This approach integrates migrants into the economy and society, promoting labor force participation and social cohesion. Conversely, solely relying on increased enforcement may address immediate security concerns but often fails to resolve underlying economic drivers of migration, leading to ongoing instability.",
